Subject: Cantor Seeded Compiler Slice 3 Attention Backend Activation Review

@ [review_uuid] a640a77a-6dc2-44bd-915e-e4a8445e9a49
@ [source_uuid] 035cb434-0810-40e1-9875-cdaefd9c140c

& [Delineation]
  + Slice2 semantic IR describes selected meaning while CPPE ProcedureCandidate describes executable control form
  + the adapter proves correspondence between them but does not invent the procedure control graph
  + compilation produces an artifact candidate identity while verification admission loading and invocation remain separate

& [Justification]
  + the existing CPPE compiler already gives deterministic normalized candidate to Process IR compilation with explicit receipts
  + a narrow lineage and anchor adapter reuses that hardened implementation instead of creating a second attention procedure language
  + this is the first place the three-backend architecture should emit a candidate because its exact compiler dependency already exists

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + request owns exact lineage candidate validation receipt node-anchor map unresolved and non-authority
  + projection owns replayed inputs CPPE outcome residuals non-authority and digest
  + correspondence is exact over package version digest and one admitted clause source identity
  + maps and existing normalized machine forms preserve deterministic replay

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [divergent] alternatives were automatic control-flow synthesis textual procedure parsing new attention bytecode or direct compilation of semantic nodes
  + [convergent] explicit normalized ProcedureCandidate plus complete semantic-anchor correspondence is the smallest honest composition
  + [holistic] this exposes the entire semantic-plan-to-procedure-candidate seam without collapsing authorship validation compilation verification admission and execution

& [SevenFoldExplosion]
  + Honesty prevents semantic IR or compilation success from claiming behavioral correctness or execution authority
  + Security pins seed plan IR anchor candidate receipt capability and pure-effect walls
  + Weaver maps every semantic node to a concrete procedure anchor and preserves both representations
  + Planner orders validation correspondence CPPE compilation projection verification and later admission
  + Refiner reuses the existing compiler and refuses automatic procedure authorship in this slice
  + Scribe binds exact mapping receipts Process IR procedure identity residuals and digests
  + Observer closes only after positive negative compatibility and workspace evidence agree

& [RiskReview]
  + mapping only package identity without clause identity could misattribute meaning and is rejected
  + accepting extra unmapped procedure anchors could smuggle undeclared semantics and must refuse or remain explicitly unresolved
  + treating a passed validation receipt as verification or admission would collapse authorities and is rejected
  + compiler composition grants no model attention access or effect execution

& [Decision]
  + activate a pure attention backend adapter around the existing CPPE compiler
  + retain explicit ProcedureCandidate authorship as a supplied dependency for later semantic synthesis work
